 Miro and files from Figma that will update in real time.",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_0:"Example PRD",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_1_0:"Notion Tip:",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_1_1:"Here at Notion we use this template to help teams plan, design and develop products with the greatest chance for success. It helps teams think through their work more deeply, improves asynchronous communication with other teams and creates space for collaboration.",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_10_0:"🛫 Plan",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0:"Example questions to answer:",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_0:"Question 1: Does everyone know what are we launching?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_0_0:"Internal alignment",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_0_0_0:"Can we explain what this change is?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_0_1_0:"Have you shared details of this change with other functions?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_1_0:"External messaging",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_1_0_0:"How are we going to communicate our launch to customers?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_0_1_1_0:"How will customers understand changes due to this launch?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1:"What are we building? How does it work? How do we know that it works? What are we measuring? When will it be ready?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_0:"Question 2: Are we sure this is going to work?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_0_0:"Quality",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_0_0_0:"Has this product been tested appropriately?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_0_1_0:"Have we checked for effects on other products?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_0_2_0:"Have we done capacity planning?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_0_3_0:"Do we have a contingency plan if the launch doesn’t go well?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_1_0:"Measurement",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_1_0_0:"Do we know how to tell if this launch is a success or not?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_1_1_1_0:"Can others see how this launch is going?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_2:"Then, answer these questions:",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_2_0:"Question 3: What are our launch steps?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_2_0_0:"Plan",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_2_0_0_0:"Have you agreed on launch audiences with PMM?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_2_0_1_0:"Did we agree on launch steps with PMM?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_11_3_0:"🚀 It’s go time!",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_12_0:"… and feel free to link to other more detailed documents",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_2_0:"👀 Problem",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_3_0:"Example questions to answer:",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_3_1:"What problem are we solving? For whom? When do they experience this issue? What data, research and feedback do we have that explains this problem? Which customers are we working with, or hearing from, to better understand this problem? Why is solving this problem urgent? Why is it important?",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_6_0:"💭 Proposal",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_7_0:"Example questions to answer:",notionDocsTutorialExamplePrd_7_1:"How are we solving this issue? What alternatives did we consider? Why did we land with this? What is the general shape of this solution? Do you have any mocks, prototypes, relevant comparisons in the market? How will we know that we’ve solved this issue? What will we measure? Have we considered how we’re building this to be fast, performant, scalable and/or relatively low-cost on our services?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_0:"Example Tech Spec",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_0_0:"Problem statement",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_1_0:"What problem are you trying to solve? If there is a PRD, this can be a sync’ed block from the PRD. Link to any other documents that are relevant for background or context.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_10_0:"Diagrams can be very helpful here.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_12_0:"What are the high level data model changes?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_13_0:"These should include any database schema changes, or any changes to structured fields, e.g. an existing JSON column.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_15_0:"What are the main changes to the UI?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_17_0:"Risks",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_18_0:"What risks might be introduced by this set of changes? Consider running a",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_18_1:"pre-mortem",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_18_2:"to raise risks. Be sure to capture mitigating these risks in the Implementation and Rollout Plans.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_2_0:"Goals",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_20_0:"Are there any backwards-incompatible changes?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_22_0:"Does this project have special implications for security and data privacy?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_24_0:"Could this change significantly increase load on any of our backend systems?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_26_0:"Does this project have any dependencies?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_28_0:"Alternative solutions",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_29_0:"What alternatives did you consider? Describe the evaluation criteria for how you chose the proposed solution.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_3_0:"What should be true after this project is implemented?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_30_0:"Implementation and rollout plan",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_31_0:"Fill this section out based on what is relevant for the size and scope of this project. This section can also be TBD as the project is started, but you should gradually fill this in as the project progresses towards launch.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_33_0:"Does this project require a migration?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_34_0:"If an extensive migration is necessary, write a separate tech spec for it and link it here. Describe how to rollback in the event of an unsuccessful migration.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_36_0:"Is this project in an experiment or feature-flagged?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_37_0:"Describe how to support an incremental release if needed.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_39_0:"Success criteria",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_4_0:"Non-goals",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_40_0:"How will you validate that the solution is working correctly?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_41_0:"Describe what automated and/or manual testing you will do. Does this project need load or stress testing? This can also be a separate Testing Plan doc that is shared with QA and linked here.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_43_0:"What monitoring and alerting will you do to ensure this project doesn’t decrease performance and reliability?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_44_0:"E.g. increased requests, latency, and error rates.",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_5_0:"What is explicitly not in scope and why?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_6_0:"Proposed solution",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_7_0:"What changes are required to solve this problem and achieve the project goals?",notionDocsTutorialExampleTechSpec_9_0:"What are the high-level architectural changes?",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_0:"Getting started with docs",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_0_0_0_0:"This Docs template helps you organise your team’s shared knowledge so you can all stay on the same page.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_1_0:"You can use Notion pages to collaborate on docs with your team, such as technical specs, architecture overviews and project kickoff notes. Each doc can be stored in this database to help your team stay organised.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_10_0:"To make it easier to create docs of the same type (such as project kickoffs or design docs), database templates let you define and replicate certain page elements with just one click.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_11_0:"To edit, install more or create your own, click on the dropdown next to the blue “New” button:",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_12_0:"Views, filters and sorts",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_13_0:"Views are customisable, flexible layouts to visualise your databases and properties as a table, board, calendar, timeline or list. This template comes with several views of docs – you can customise each or create your own!",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_14_0:"Frame 6.png",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_15_0:"Learn more about Notion’s database layouts, including when to use each type of database view, in this guide:",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_15_1:"https://www.notion.com/help/guides/when-to-use-each-type-of-database-view",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_15_2:".",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_2_0:"How to use this template",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_3_0:"This is your team’s documentation database. You can click on each item to open up its own page where you can add important information – strategy memos, product requirement docs and design critiques.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_3_0_0:"Frame 4.png",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_4_0:"Click “+ New” to add a new entry to the database.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_4_0_0:"Frame 7.png",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_5_0:"Use the view tabs to visualise your docs in different ways – like by creator or last edited date.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_6_0:"Frame 5.png",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_7_0:"Customise this template",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_8_0:"This template is pre-populated with the most common fields for docs (like creator and last edited info), but you can add your own when you add a new field.",notionDocsTutorialSimpleDocsGettingStarted_9_0:"Database templates","notionMailAccountRequiredModal.ariaLabel":"Connect your email to Notion","notionMailAccountRequir