tionMailOnboarding.insufficientOAuthScopes.title":"Gmail permissions required","notionMailOnboarding.signupError.message":"Please try again or contact support if the issue persists.","notionMailOnboarding.signupError.title":"Failed to connect Notion Mail","notionMailOnboarding.signupSuccess.message":"Your email account has been connected. You can now ask the Notion agent about your emails.","notionMailOnboarding.signupSuccess.title":"Notion Mail connected","NotionMailUniversalQnaAnnouncementModal.shortDescription":"Search and ask about your emails","NotionMailUniversalQnaAnnouncementModal.subtitleForAnnouncement":"Find information and get answers about your Notion Mail emails.","NotionMailUniversalQnaAnnouncementModal.title":"Get Notion Mail answers in Notion AI",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_0:"Getting started with meeting notes",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_0_0_0_0:"This Meetings template helps you organise your meetings in Notion, such as setting agendas and taking notes.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_1_0:"You can use Notion pages to collaborate on meeting notes with your team, such as 1:1s, standups and team meetings. Each meeting can be stored in this database to help your team stay organised.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_10_0:"To edit, install more or create your own, click on the dropdown next to the blue “New” button:",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_11_0:"Views, filters and sorts",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_12_0:"Views are customisable, flexible layouts to visualise your databases and properties as a table, board, calendar, timeline or list. This template comes with several views of meeting notes – you can customise each or create your own!",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_14_0:"Learn more about Notion’s database layouts, including when to use each type of database view, in this guide:",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_2_0:"How to use this template",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_3_0:"This is your team’s meeting notes database. You can click on each item to open up its own page where you can add categorical information, create an agenda and record action items – right alongside your teammates.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_4_0:"Click “+ New” to add an upcoming meeting to the database.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_5_0:"Use the view tabs to visualise your meeting notes in different ways – like by date, by type, or filtered to only include the ones you’ve attended.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_6_0:"Customise this template",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_7_0:"This template is pre-populated with the most common meeting notes fields (like attendees and meeting date), but you can add your own when you add in a new field/column.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_8_0:"Database templates",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsGettingStartedWithMeetings_9_0:"To make it easier to create meetings of the same type (such as bug reports and design specs), database templates let you define and replicate certain page elements with just one click.",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamStandupPage_0:"Team standup",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamStandupPage_0_0:"Discussion topics",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamStandupPage_1_0:"…",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamStandupPage_3_0:"Team updates",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamStandupPage_4_0:"Add my update",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_0:"Team weekly",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_0_0:"📚 Pre-read",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_1_0:"Docs",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_1_0_0:"Add your docs here…",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_2_0:"Team updates & gut checks",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_2_0_0:"Add your team members’ updates and gut checks here…",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_3_0:"📣 Agenda items",notionMeetingsTutorialMeetingsTeamWeeklyPage_5_0:"☑️ Action items",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage1:"Add a new task",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage1_0:"Ready to start tracking your tasks here? Start by clicking the blue “New” button at the top right of your table.",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage1_1:"Customise each task by populating the fields above, such as the task’s assignee, due date and status.",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage1AiSummary:"This document provides instructions for adding a new task to a task tracking system. The task ID, assignee, status, due date, priority and tags can be customised for each task.",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage2:"Invite team members",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage2_0:"Ready to collaborate with your team? Use the Share menu in the top right.",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage2_1:"Use the “Assignee” field above to assign tasks to your teammates. They’ll see a notification in their sidebar.",notionProjectsTutorial_getStartedTasksPage2AiSummary:"This document provides instructions for inviting team members to collaborate on a task. Use the Share menu to invite team members and assign tasks using the “Assignee” field. Team members will receive a notification in their sidebar.",notionProjectsTutorial_planning:"Planning",notionProjectsTutorial_project1:"Sample project: Performance",notionProjectsTutorial_project1_heading0:"About this project",notionProjectsTutorial_project1_heading1:"Performance dashboards",notionProjectsTutorial_project1_heading2:"Project tasks",notionProjectsTutorial_project1_paragraph0:"Last year, the team prioritised mobile performance and successfully reduced page load times by 50%. This directly correlated with increased mobile usage and more positive app store reviews.",notionProjectsTutorial_project1_paragraph1:"This quarter, the mobile team is doubling down on performance and investing in more native components across iOS and Android.",notionProjectsTutorial_project1AiSummary:"The mobile team is prioritising performance and investing in more native components across iOS and Android. Last year, the team successfully reduced page load times by 50%, leading to increased mobile usage and positive app store reviews. The project is currently in the planning stage, with performance dashboards and project tasks to be developed.",notionProjectsTutorial_project2:"Sample project: User education",notionProjectsTutorial_project2_heading1:"Proposed user journey",notionProjectsTutorial_project2_paragraph0:"Because our app has so many features and serves so many personas and use cases, many users find the current onboarding process overwhelming and don’t experience their “aha” moment quickly enough.",notionProjectsTutorial_project2_paragraph1:"This quarter, the user education team is investing in a holistically redesigned onboarding flow, with a goal of increasing 7-day retention by 25%.",notionProjectsTutorial_project2AiSummary:"The user education team is planning a project to redesign the onboarding flow for their app, with the goal of increasing 7-day retention by 25%. The current onboarding process is overwhelming for many users, and the team aims to create a more effective user journey. The project is scheduled to take place from 8 May 2023 to 4 June 2023.",notionProjectsTutorial_sprint1:"Sprint 1",notionProjectsTutorial_sprint2:"Sprint 2",notionProjectsTutorial_sprint3:"Sprint 3",notionProjectsTutorial_task1:"Write project proposal",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_0:"Goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_0_0:"Achieve cross-functional alignment on why and how we’re investing in mobile performance in Q3",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_0_1:"Include more user stories and specific problem statements, and be clear about what’s not in scope for now",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_1:"Non-goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_1_0:"Get explicit leadership sign-off",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_1_1:"Synthesise user research learnings (already captured in research team’s performance doc)",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_2:"Next steps:",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_2_0:"Gather feedback from mobile team",notionProjectsTutorial_task1_2_1:"Work with internal comms to create awareness in the appropriate Slack channels",notionProjectsTutorial_task1AiSummary:"This project proposal aims to achieve cross-functional alignment on investing in mobile performance in Q3. Goals include adding user stories and specific problem statements, while non-goals include getting leadership sign-off and synthesising user research learnings. Next steps include gathering feedback from the mobile team and creating awareness in appropriate Slack channels with internal comms.",notionProjectsTutorial_task2:"Schedule kick-off meeting",notionProjectsTutorial_task2AiSummary:"This task is in progress and involves scheduling a kick-off meeting for the performance project, preparing meeting materials in advance, and inviting all stakeholders to the meeting. Non-goals include brainstorming additional performance projects. The due date is 26 April 2023 and the priority is medium. The task is tagged as “Mobile”.",notionProjectsTutorial_task3:"Review research results",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_0:"Goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_0_0:"Understand which product areas need most education",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_0_1:"Deprioritise product areas that already see high engagement",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_1:"Non-goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_1_0:"Recommend UI changes for core product",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_1_1:"Recommend changes to product roadmap",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_2:"Next steps:",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_2_0:"Watch all 10 interviews from research team",notionProjectsTutorial_task3_2_1:"Write up insights and share in Slack",notionProjectsTutorial_task3AiSummary:"This document outlines the goals and non-goals for a research task, which include understanding which product areas need more education and deprioritising areas with high engagement. The next steps involve watching 10 interviews and sharing insights in Slack.",notionProjectsTutorial_task4:"Build data dashboards",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_0:"Goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_0_0:"Give cross-functional partners the ability to self-serve info about tooltip effectiveness among new user cohorts",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_0_1:"Measure activation and retention against control group",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_1:"Non-goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_1_0:"Add new events to track new feature adoption",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_1_1:"Track how often tooltips are skipped (blocked for now)",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_2:"Next steps:",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_2_0:"Ask Jonny for access to Hex",notionProjectsTutorial_task4_2_1:"Schedule cross-functional meeting to collect any remaining feedback and requests",notionProjectsTutorial_task4AiSummary:"This task is to build data dashboards for measuring activation and retention against control groups and giving cross-functional partners the ability to self-serve information about tooltip effectiveness among new user cohorts. Next steps include asking Jonny for access to Hex and scheduling a cross-functional meeting for feedback and requests. The non-goal is to track how often tooltips are skipped.",notionProjectsTutorial_task5:"Scope tooltip project",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_0:"Goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_0_0:"Uncover any technical blockers to building education tooltips",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_0_1:"Estimate how long engineering will need to build tooltips",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_1:"Non-goals:",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_1_0:"Evaluate new events for data team to track",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_1_1:"Collect feedback from cross-functional partners",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_2:"Next steps:",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_2_0:"Revisit docs from previous Q1 tooltip project",notionProjectsTutorial_task5_2_1:"Write tech spec and share to product team email alias",notionProjectsTutorial_task5AiSummary:"This document outlines the scope of the tooltip project, including goals of uncovering technical blockers and estimating engineering time, as well as non-goals of evaluating new events and collecting feedback. The next steps include revisiting docs from a previous project and writing a tech spec to share with the product team email alias.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_0:"Getting started with projects, tasks & sprints",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_0_0_0_0:"Learn how to organise tasks by project, coordinate with your team and track progress.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_1_0:"How to use this template",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_10_0:"Projects are typically made up of tasks. A project represents a large body of work such as a product launch or team milestone. A project can be broken down into many tasks and can contain customisable properties such as status.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_11_0:"Sprints",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_12_0:"Sprints are another dimension by which you can organise tasks and projects, commonly used in Agile workflows. A sprint represents a discrete cycle of time in which tasks will be completed. You can configure start and end dates per sprint and assign each task to a sprint.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_13_0:"Adding custom fields",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_14_0:"We’ve pre-populated this template with the most common project management fields (like task status and assignee), but you can add your own when you are creating a new field. You’ll have options like priority, estimates and task type.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_16_0:"Template settings really just toggle different database properties on and off. Learn more about database properties here:",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_17_0:"Views, filters and sorts",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_18_0:"Views are customisable, flexible layouts to visualise your databases and properties as a table, board, calendar, timeline or list. This template comes with several views of projects, tasks and sprints – you can customise each or create your own!",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_2_0:"This is your sample project tracker. It contains projects, tasks and sprints – you can click on the name of the project or task to open up its own page where you can add new detail.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_20_0:"Learn more about Notion’s database layouts, including when to use each type of database view, in this guide:",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_20_2:".",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_3_0:"Click “+ New” below the sample tasks to add a new task.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_4_0:"Navigate views using tabs at the top of the database – each one uses the same underlying data but displays it in different ways so that you can quickly and easily keep track of all your team’s happenings.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_5_0:"Tasks, sprints and projects",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_6_0:"We’ve pre-populated your template with different types of information housed in databases. Databases in Notion are collections of pages. In our case, projects and tasks are each their own",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_6_1:"database",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_6_2:". Learn more about the general structure of a database, walk through the different menus and options, and deep-dive into how to open and edit pages within a database",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_7_0:"Tasks",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_8_0:"Tasks are the smallest unit of work in your project management tracker. A task represents a more granular piece of work, often assigned to just one person. Many tasks can be organised into a project or added to a sprint.",notionProjectsTutorialAgileGettingStartedWithProjects_9_0:"Projects",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_0:"Getting started with projects, tasks & sprints",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_0_0:"Notion tip: This guide is also a fully functional projects page. Try changing properties or adding tasks to see how your workspace changes.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_2_0:"Sprints in Notion are built with four core concepts",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_3_0:"Projects —",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_3_1:"Each project opens into its own page (like this one!) where you can add tasks and project details. All of your projects are also housed in your newly created Projects page.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_4_0:"Tasks —",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_4_1:"All of your tasks live in the Tasks page. Like projects, tasks open as their own pages where you can add subtasks and assign them to projects. They can also be assigned to sprints.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_5_0:"Sprints —",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_5_1:"Sprints are measurements of time that can contain any number of tasks. You can view and assign tasks to sprints on your Sprints page or on any task page.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_6_0:"Sprint board —",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_6_0_0:"Plus, use the sprint board to complete sprints automatically",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_6_0_0_0:"On your sprint board, click the Complete sprint button to automatically move incomplete tasks and start your next sprint.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_6_1:"The Sprint board combines all of the concepts listed above so that you can view your tasks grouped by project and filtered according to your current sprint.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_7_0:"Learn more",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_8_0:"You can customise your project and task setup to match your team’s style of work. Learn more in our",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_8_1:"help centre →",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithAgileV2_AiSummary:"This page outlines how to use the four core concepts in Notion for sprint planning: projects, tasks, sprints and the Sprint board. It also provides a brief guide for completing sprints and links to Notion’s help centre for more details.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_0:"Getting started with projects & tasks",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_0_0_0_0:"Learn how to organise tasks by project, coordinate with your team and track progress.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_1_0:"How to use this template",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_10_0:"Projects are typically made up of tasks. A project represents a large body of work such as a product launch or team milestone. A project can be broken down into many tasks and can contain customisable properties such as status.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_11_0:"Adding custom fields",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_12_0:"We’ve pre-populated this template with the most common project management fields (like task status and assignee), but you can add your own when you are creating a new field. You’ll have options like priority, estimates and task type.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_14_0:"Learn more about database properties here:",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_15_0:"Views, filters and sorts",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_16_0:"Views are customisable, flexible layouts to visualise your databases and properties as a table, board, calendar, timeline or list. This template comes with several views of projects and tasks – you can customise each or create your own!",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_18_0:"Learn more about Notion’s database layouts, including when to use each type of database view, in this guide:",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_18_2:".",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_2_0:"This is your sample project tracker. It contains projects and tasks – you can click on the name of the project or task to open up its own page where you can add new detail.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_3_0:"Click “+ New” below the sample tasks to add a new task.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_4_0:"Navigate views using tabs at the top of the database – each one uses the same underlying data but displays it in different ways so that you can quickly and easily keep track of all your team’s happenings.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_5_0:"Tasks and projects",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_6_0:"We’ve pre-populated your template with different types of information housed in databases. Databases in Notion are collections of pages. In our case, projects and tasks are each their own",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_6_1:"database",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_6_2:". Learn more about the general structure of a database, walk through the different menus and options, and deep-dive into how to open and edit pages within a database",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_6_3:"here.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_7_0:"Tasks",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_8_0:"Tasks are the smallest unit of work in your project management tracker. A task represents a more granular piece of work, often assigned to just one person. Many tasks can be organised into a project.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjects_9_0:"Projects",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsAiSummary:"This document provides an introduction to organising tasks, projects and sprints using a project management tracker. It explains how to use the provided template, add custom fields and customise views. Tasks are the smallest unit of work, projects represent larger bodies of work, and sprints are discrete cycles of time for completing tasks. The template includes common fields like task status and assignee, but users can add their own fields like priority and task type.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_0:"Getting started with projects & tasks",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_0_0:"Notion tip: This guide is also a fully functional project page. Try changing properties or adding tasks to see how your setup changes.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_1_0:"Projects and tasks are built with four core concepts",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_3_0:"Projects —",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_3_1:"Each project has its own page (like this one!) where you can add tasks and project details. All of your projects are also housed in your newly created Projects page.",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_4_0:"Tasks —",notionProjectsTutorialProjectsGettingStartedWithProjectsV2_4_1:"All of your tasks live in the Tasks page. Like projects, tasks o